            <ArticleTitle>Nephrogenic fibrosing dermopathy: two pediatric cases.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>678-81</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report two pediatric cases of nephrogenic fibrosing dermopathy (NFD), first described in 2000. NFD is a condition in which individuals with renal dysfunction have development of extensive skin hardening and histopathologic evidence of a scleromyxedema-like condition.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
